From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 23:47:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] RIL: answer setDataProfile at once when IRadio 1.0-1.3 gets
 nothing to send

For HIDL IRadio below 1.4, RadioDataProxy.setDataProfile() forwards only
persistent (modem cognitive) profiles and does not call the HAL at all when
none is persistent. RIL.setDataProfile() has already obtained a RILRequest
by then, so that request is never answered: it stays in mRequestList
holding the RIL wakelock until WAKE_LOCK_TIMEOUT, on every data profile
update.

On the Meizu MX6 (IRadio 1.1) none of the SIM's data profiles is
persistent, and each SET_DATA_PROFILE ends 60 s later as

  RILJ: WAKE_LOCK_TIMEOUT  mRequestList=2
  RILJ: 0: [164] SET_DATA_PROFILE / 1: [206] SET_DATA_PROFILE

while the vendor RIL never logs "onRequest: SET_DATA_PROFILE", because the
request never leaves the framework. Android 11 did not have the leak: there
the RILRequest was obtained only when the persistent list was non-empty;
the Android 13 split into RadioDataProxy moved obtainRequest() ahead of the
filter.

RadioDataProxy.hasDataProfilesToSend() states the filter, and RIL completes
the request immediately when it is false. The result is success: there is
nothing to program into the modem (DataProfileManager passes no completion
message anyway; CellularDataService would map any exception to
RESULT_ERROR_ILLEGAL_STATE). AIDL and IRadio >= 1.4 are unchanged.

Change-Id: I8387fef092328a9d296f0d153aafdc98f2ecaa07

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java
index 70431f6..23d541e 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java
@@ -4162,6 +4162,22 @@ public class RIL extends BaseCommands implements CommandsInterface {
     public void setDataProfile(DataProfile[] dps, boolean isRoaming, Message result) {
         RadioDataProxy dataProxy = getRadioServiceProxy(RadioDataProxy.class, result);
         if (!dataProxy.isEmpty()) {
+            if (!dataProxy.hasDataProfilesToSend(dps)) {
+                // IRadio 1.0-1.3 carries persistent profiles only, and RadioDataProxy skips the
+                // HAL call when there is none. A RILRequest obtained here would never be answered:
+                // it would sit in mRequestList holding the RIL wakelock until WAKE_LOCK_TIMEOUT,
+                // on every data profile update. There is nothing to program into the modem, so
+                // complete the request now.
+                if (RILJ_LOGD) {
+                    riljLog("setDataProfile: no persistent data profile for IRadio "
+                            + mRadioVersion + ", nothing to send");
+                }
+                if (result != null) {
+                    AsyncResult.forMessage(result, null, null);
+                    result.sendToTarget();
+                }
+                return;
+            }
             RILRequest rr = obtainRequest(RIL_REQUEST_SET_DATA_PROFILE, result,
                     mRILDefaultWorkSource);
 
diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioDataProxy.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioDataProxy.java
index cbc762a..0f06e88 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioDataProxy.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RadioDataProxy.java
@@ -202,6 +202,22 @@ public class RadioDataProxy extends RadioServiceProxy {
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Whether {@link #setDataProfile} would reach the HAL for these profiles. IRadio 1.0 to 1.3
+     * carry only persistent (modem cognitive) profiles, and the HAL is not called at all when
+     * none of the given profiles is persistent.
+     * @param profiles The data profiles about to be sent
+     * @return false if setDataProfile would send nothing
+     */
+    public boolean hasDataProfilesToSend(DataProfile[] profiles) {
+        if (isEmpty()) return false;
+        if (isAidl() || mHalVersion.greaterOrEqual(RIL.RADIO_HAL_VERSION_1_4)) return true;
+        for (DataProfile dp : profiles) {
+            if (dp.isPersistent()) return true;
+        }
+        return false;
+    }
+
     /**
      * Call IRadioData#setDataProfile
      * @param serial Serial number of request
